@startuml component-diagram
title Route Optimization Platform - Component Diagram (Static View)

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam wrapWidth 200
skinparam shadowing false

actor "API Client" as Client
actor "Developer (CLI)" as Developer

package "API Layer" {
  [Flask API\n(Web/app.py)] as API
  [Validator\n(Web/validator.py)] as Validator
}

package "CP-SAT Pipeline (single production pipeline)" {
  [Orchestrator\n(CP-SAT/main.py)] as MainOrchestrator
  [Vehicle Routes Solver\n(CP-SAT/vehicle_routes.py)] as VehicleRoutesSolver
  [Loader Routes Solver\n(CP-SAT/loader_routes.py)] as LoaderRoutesSolver
  [Common Utils\n(CP-SAT/common_functions.py)] as CommonUtils
}

package "Shared" {
  [Models / Dataclasses\n(Shared/models.py)] as Models
  [Verifier\n(Shared/verifier.py)] as Verifier
  [History\n(Shared/history.py)] as History
  database "Data Storage\n(input/output.json,\nlive scratch files)" as DataStorage
  folder "Per-calculation snapshots\n(data/inputs/{id}.json,\ndata/outputs/{id}.json)" as Snapshots
  database "history.db\n(SQLite, calculation_history)" as HistoryDB
}

package "Offline Tools" {
  [Tester\n(tester.py)] as Tester
  folder "instances/\n(TASK.json, output_TASK.json)" as TestCases
  file "comparison.xlsx" as ComparisonFile
  [Solution Validator CLI\n(Validator class in Web/validator.py)] as OfflineValidator
}

Models -[hidden]d-> Developer

Client --> API : POST /solve, GET /solution\nPOST /validate, GET /metrics\nGET /history, GET /history/{id}
API --> Validator : validate_input()
API --> History : start_calculation()\nfinish_success() / finish_error()\nget_all() / get_by_id()
History --> HistoryDB : SQL read/write
History --> Snapshots : write input/output\nJSON per calculation_id
API --> MainOrchestrator : solve_pipeline()
MainOrchestrator --> VehicleRoutesSolver
MainOrchestrator --> LoaderRoutesSolver
VehicleRoutesSolver --> CommonUtils
LoaderRoutesSolver --> CommonUtils
MainOrchestrator --> Models
VehicleRoutesSolver --> Models
LoaderRoutesSolver --> Models
MainOrchestrator --> DataStorage : read input.json\nwrite output.json
MainOrchestrator --> Verifier : run_verification()
API --> DataStorage : read output.json\n(GET /metrics, no orchestrator call)

Developer --> Tester : python tester.py
Tester ..> TestCases : reads (baseline is a\nstatic file, not live PyVRP)
Tester ..> ComparisonFile : appends sheet
Developer --> OfflineValidator : python validator.py --dir ...
OfflineValidator ..> TestCases : reads input/result/\nbaseline files
OfflineValidator ..> ComparisonFile : appends sheet\n(separate report,\nnot code-shared with Verifier)

note bottom of VehicleRoutesSolver
  Pool via Clarke-Wright + randomized insertion
  (optionally seeded once by a one-time OR-Tools
  run, reused by every attempt). CP-SAT selects
  the optimal subset via set-partitioning.
  Post-processing: consolidate_routes(),
  reduce_vehicles_by_merge(),
  inter_route_local_search(),
  merge_multi_trip_routes().
end note

note bottom of MainOrchestrator
  Runs a multi-start loop: independent full
  attempts, keeps the one with lowest real
  total_cost, then an LNS polish phase
  (perturb + re-improve) with remaining time.
  Feedback iteration drops optional orders
  unprofitable on BOTH the vehicle side (exact
  marginal savings) and loader side, re-selects
  from the same pool. One shared deadline
  (max_total_time, default 840s), budgets
  scaled by instance size - see ADR-005, ADR-008.
end note

note bottom of Verifier
  Used only by this pipeline now that Pipeline B
  (PyVRP) has been removed - see ADR-001.
  Verifies shift times, time windows, and
  vehicle capacity against the solution.
end note

note right of OfflineValidator
  Independent of Shared/verifier.py: its own
  constraint checks, baseline comparison, and
  Excel export. Not wired to the Flask app.
end note

note right of History
  Records one row per /solve call: timestamp,
  execution_time, objective_function_cost,
  status (processing/success/error), and paths
  to the per-calculation input/output snapshots.
  See ADR-007. Only used by the API layer.
end note

@enduml
